{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>Torn I did not bring to you.</b> Even if it was torn under duress, I was exempt by law, as it is written יביאהו עד, and our Sages said: he must bring witnesses that it was torn under duress and he is exempt. Even that I did not bring to you in order to be exempt, but rather I paid for it from my own. <b>I stole a day and I stole a night</b> — it is the shepherd's custom to graze by day and by night to return the flock to the owner's pen. And if it was stolen at night, it was stolen from its owner, but I — <b>from my hand you would seek it</b> — stolen by day or stolen by night, it is upon me to pay."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "The repeated word גנבתי in the Hebrew may be read as 'I stole (from you)' in the first clause and '(it was) stolen' in the second; the translation preserves the shepherd's first-person voice throughout."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:58.684791519Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}